A Precept is a general rule, tenet or doctrine intended to regulate behaviour or thought.

The Precept Bible is based on the understanding of the scripture in Isaiah 28:9-10 where it clearly states how scriptures will be taught in the last days. The children of the promise would have forgotten their heritage and identity and all the history that they ought to have known.

They would now require some extensive hand-holding as they are taken from passage to passage, and the understanding of each line of scripture is ellucidated and taught to them precept by precept.

If you want to understand the bible, you will need to be guided by the precepts, which are the keys to unlocking the meanings and intents of its passages in context. Let scripture interpret scripture.

START LEARNING PRECEPTS NOW!
- Start by reading the verses and passages related to each precept;
- Get the understanding of the precept by reading the cross-linked verses;
- You begin to see the consistency in scripture when you realise that certain words and phrases maintain specific meaning in all the verses they appear in;
- Connect the dots and you begin to see the bigger picture of what the bible is really revealing.

MORE FEATURES WITH EACH UPDATE
- Easy navigation for chapters and verses;
- Quickly check up on precepts listed under a verse, and link to cross-linked verses;
- Adjust font sizes for accessibility;
- Use the contact form to send us messages and what you've discovered;
- Join our mailing list and get updates about our occasional updates and learning aids;

REDISCOVER THE CORRECT WAY TO UNDERSTAND SCRIPTURE
- Build up entire teaching series using bible precepts to maintain true scriptural meanings and consistency in the understanding delivered.

Join us on social media and share the gospel to wake up the lost sheep!
Share this app with friends and family and be part of their awakening.

Containing more than 330,000 translations, this is the most comprehensive offline English and Portuguese bilingual dictionary. Made with scientific and lexicographical rigor, the "Michaelis Moderno Dicionário Inglês" is up-to-date with neologisms and the newest technical terms of areas such as Computing, Economics, Marketing, Arts, Communication, Sciences, Technology etc.

The contents of the entire dictionary follows the Portuguese Language Orthographic Vocabulary (VOLP, 5th edition, March 2009), respecting the changes introduced by the Portuguese Language Orthographic Agreement of 1990.

The application was created using state-of-the-art technology, presenting results immediately when querying for a word, with a clean and objective user interface optimized for iPhone/iPod and iPad users.

Get the complete contents of the printed edition, with the same quality and presentation, and requiring only a small space in your gadget!

The main features of "Michaelis Moderno Dicionário Inglês" are:

• complete contents without requiring Internet connection;
• more than 330,000 translations;
• more than 350,000 expressions and examples;
• audible speaking of all words via TTS;
• syllable division of the entries;
• part of speech of words and government of verbs;
• references to more than 100 areas of knowledge;
• idiomatic expressions, proverbs and slang;
• plurals, feminines, irregular augmentatives and diminutives;
• complete conjugation of all Portuguese and English verbs in the dictionary;
• synonyms and variants;
• extra texts:
  – tables of mathematical symbols and numbers;
  – conversion tables of weights and measures;
  – gender, collective and voices of animals;
  – proverbs and popular sayings;
  – Practical Guide of the Portuguese Language Orthographic Agreement;
• definition lookup from other apps;
• advanced query for Portuguese by spelling approximation;
• automatic recognition of almost 1,000,000 verb conjugations;
• recognition of plurals, feminines, superlatives, augmentatives and diminutives;
• query by beginning, ending, or middle of entry or by definition of the entry;
• option to configure the colors of information displayed;
• history, bookmarks and index of entries;

A valuable tool to improve the knowledge of the English language.
